From ac722dd8a68cc904d814c5d68b28d8acae9858d0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 10:42:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(ci): make Studio deploy workflow actually install & run
 in studio/
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The Deploy Sanity Studio workflow (deploy-studio.yml) failed on its
first real run: "sh: 1: sanity: not found" / "Local package.json
exists, but node_modules missing, did you mean to install?".

Root cause: studio/ is NOT a member of the root pnpm-workspace.yaml
(which only lists '.'). Without --ignore-workspace, pnpm run from
inside studio/ walks up, finds the repo root's workspace file, and
silently installs into the REPO ROOT's node_modules instead of
studio's — confirmed by reproducing locally: `pnpm install
--frozen-lockfile` from studio/ created node_modules at the repo root,
leaving studio/node_modules (and its `sanity` binary) missing entirely.
Fixed by adding --ignore-workspace to both the install and deploy
steps.

That surfaced a second, pre-existing bug once the install actually
targeted studio/: studio/pnpm-lock.yaml was stale — its importers
block was missing @sanity/client and @sanity/image-url entirely, even
though studio/package.json has declared both since the CMS work
earlier this session (lockfile was probably last regenerated by `npm
install`, which touches studio/package-lock.json, not the pnpm one).
That drift breaks `--frozen-lockfile` outright. Regenerated
studio/pnpm-lock.yaml with `pnpm install --ignore-workspace` (no
source changes needed — @sanity/image-url isn't actually imported
anywhere in studio/, so this was previously silently resolving to a
stale transitive 1.2.0 instead of the declared ^2.1.1).

Verified locally end to end: `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile
--ignore-workspace` now correctly populates studio/node_modules
(3–10s, not the suspiciously-instant no-op the old broken path gave),
`pnpm --ignore-workspace run deploy` now correctly resolves and runs
the `sanity` binary (fails only on missing login/token, as expected
outside CI), and the Studio still builds cleanly (`sanity build`).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_012xNEugH42JGJDBqiHFtfyU
---
 .github/workflows/deploy-studio.yml | 13 ++++-
 studio/pnpm-lock.yaml               | 89 ++++++++++++++++++-----------
 2 files changed, 65 insertions(+), 37 deletions(-)

diff --git a/.github/workflows/deploy-studio.yml b/.github/workflows/deploy-studio.yml
index 264e675..efc3baa 100644
--- a/.github/workflows/deploy-studio.yml
+++ b/.github/workflows/deploy-studio.yml
@@ -46,14 +46,21 @@ jobs:
           cache-dependency-path: studio/pnpm-lock.yaml
 
       # ── 4. Install dependencies ──
+      # --ignore-workspace: studio/ is a standalone project with its own
+      # lockfile, NOT a member of the root pnpm-workspace.yaml (which only
+      # lists '.'). Without this flag pnpm walks up, finds the repo root's
+      # workspace file, and silently installs into the repo root's
+      # node_modules instead of studio's — leaving studio/node_modules
+      # missing and `sanity` unresolved ("sh: 1: sanity: not found").
       - name: Install dependencies
-        run: pnpm install --frozen-lockfile
+        run: pnpm install --frozen-lockfile --ignore-workspace
 
       # ── 5. Deploy Studio to sanity.studio ──
       # sanity.cli.ts already pins studioHost + projectId, so this runs
       # fully non-interactively as long as SANITY_AUTH_TOKEN is set — no
-      # prompts for hostname or project selection.
+      # prompts for hostname or project selection. --ignore-workspace for
+      # the same reason as the install step above.
       - name: Deploy Studio
         env:
           SANITY_AUTH_TOKEN: ${{ secrets.SANITY_DEPLOY_TOKEN }}
-        run: pnpm run deploy
+        run: pnpm --ignore-workspace run deploy
